ediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKABAYASHI, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHUTO, KENSHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KEN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A wound-covering preparation containing a polymer having a group represented by formula (I) (wherein R&lt;1&gt;, R&lt;2&gt;, and R&lt;3&gt; are the same or different and each represents hydrogen or C1-4 alkyl, and m is an integer of 2 to 4); a wound-covering material containing the preparation; and a method of wound healing which comprises the step of covering the wound of a patient with the wound-covering material to protect the wound.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une préparation pour pansement, qui comprend un polymère renfermant un groupe représenté par la formule (I), dans laquelle R&lt;1&gt;, R&lt;2&gt; et R&lt;3&gt;, identiques ou différents, représentent hydrogène ou alkyle C1-C4, et m est un entier compris entre 2 et 4; un matériau pour pansement, contenant ladite préparation; et un méthode de traitement des plaies qui comprend une étape consistant à recouvrir la plaie d'un patient avec ledit matériau afin de la protéger.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms a